> According to Variety, one of the movies about the 1973 tennis match between Billie Jean King and Bobby Riggs is recasting[ one] of its leads. No, not the serious one that HBO is doing with Elizabeth Banks and Paul G[iam]atti, and not the overtly comedic one that Will Fer[rell] is set to star in. It’s Battle Of The Sexes, the middle one that’s supposed to be a comedy[ with] “dramatic[ and] political overtones”—[as] we said in an earlier report. Battle Of The Sexes comes from Little Miss Sunshine’s Jonathan Dayton and Valerie Faris, and it was set to star Emma Stone and Steve Carell[ as] the eponymous sexes. Now, Stone has backed out due to “a scheduling conflict,” and the studio is reportedly in talks with Brie Larson to replace her.
